---
description: Preserve signed commits when sandboxed git cannot reach GPG
alwaysApply: true
---
# Signed commit handling

- Keep signed commits enabled when the user requests commits.
- If `git commit` fails in the sandbox with GPG or keybox access errors, retry the same commit outside the sandbox so the local signing setup can run normally.
- Do not work around this by using `--no-gpg-sign`, disabling signing, or changing git config.
- Prefer a broader-permission retry only for the commit step that actually needs local GPG access.
